{{- /*
The account-wide deny rules for the two plugin hosts, which name the file
differently and read the same shape into it: ~/.config/opencode/opencode.json
for opencode, ~/.config/kilo/kilo.json for Kilo Code.  One asset rather than two
identical ones, these having already been kept in step by hand.  Should the two
shapes ever diverge, split this back into a file each rather than adding a knob.

GENERATED.  The paths come from internal/install/protectedpaths.go, written
once and rendered into each agent's own spelling; nothing here is a path of its
own.  Add one there.

Deny rules only, and no catch-all.  The last matching wildcard wins and the
merge re-serialises with keys sorted, so an operator's rule sorting after one of
these takes effect; sorting puts a catch-all first, and there is no default this
is entitled to replace.

read and edit take the same list.  A value the agent cannot read is one it can
still destroy, and an age key replaced is every managed file unreadable
retroactively.
*/ -}}
{
  "permission": {
    "read": {
{{ jsonDenyMap "      " (pluginPatterns .) }}
    },
    "edit": {
{{ jsonDenyMap "      " (pluginPatterns .) }}
    }
  }
}
